@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Integrating Azure Artifacts with CI/CD";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="lead text-center">Learn how to integrate Azure Artifacts into Continuous Integration and Continuous Deployment (CI/CD) pipelines for efficient package management and deployment.</p>
    <hr />

    <!-- Introduction -->
    <div class="mt-4">
        <h2 class="text-success">What is Azure Artifacts?</h2>
        <p>
            Azure Artifacts is a powerful package management service within Azure DevOps that enables teams to create, host, and share packages such as NuGet, npm, Maven, and Python.
            It facilitates seamless package dependency management across CI/CD pipelines, improving development efficiency and security.
        </p>
        <p>
            With Azure Artifacts, teams can integrate package feeds into their CI/CD workflows, ensuring that applications always use the latest stable versions of dependencies.
        </p>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/azure-artifacts-overview.jpg" alt="Azure Artifacts Overview" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Azure Artifacts streamlines package management and enhances build automation.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Benefits of Using Azure Artifacts in CI/CD -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-warning">Benefits of Azure Artifacts in CI/CD</h2>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Secure Package Storage:</strong> Store private and public packages with built-in security and access controls.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Seamless Integration:</strong> Works effortlessly with Azure Pipelines for automated builds and deployments.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Version Control:</strong> Manage package versions and track changes over time.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Cross-Team Collaboration:</strong> Share packages across multiple teams in a controlled and efficient manner.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Support for Multiple Package Types:</strong> Compatible with NuGet, npm, Maven, Python, and Universal Packages.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/benefits-azure-artifacts.jpg" alt="Benefits of Azure Artifacts" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Azure Artifacts ensures secure and scalable package management.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Step-by-Step Integration Guide -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-danger">How to Integrate Azure Artifacts with CI/CD</h2>
        <ol class="list-group list-group-numbered">
            <li class="list-group-item">Create an Azure Artifacts feed in Azure DevOps.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Configure your development environment to connect to the Artifacts feed.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Publish packages to the Artifacts feed from your local or CI/CD pipeline.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Update your build pipeline to restore dependencies from Azure Artifacts.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Ensure versioning and security policies are enforced within the pipeline.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Deploy applications using the packages stored in Azure Artifacts.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/integration-steps.jpg" alt="Steps to Integrate Azure Artifacts" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Follow these steps to integrate Azure Artifacts into your CI/CD pipeline.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Best Practices for Azure Artifacts Integration -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-info">Best Practices for Using Azure Artifacts</h2>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Use Scoped Feeds:</strong> Organize packages based on projects and teams for better access control.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Implement Dependency Caching:</strong> Reduce build times by caching frequently used dependencies.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Automate Package Versioning:</strong> Ensure consistency with automated versioning in CI/CD pipelines.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Monitor Package Usage:</strong> Regularly audit package consumption to maintain security and compliance.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Enable Retention Policies:</strong> Remove outdated packages automatically to optimize storage.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/best-practices-artifacts.jpg" alt="Best Practices for Azure Artifacts" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Following best practices improves efficiency and security in CI/CD pipelines.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Conclusion -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-secondary">Conclusion</h2>
        <p>
            Integrating Azure Artifacts into CI/CD pipelines enhances software development by ensuring secure, efficient, and automated package management.
            By leveraging best practices and seamless Azure DevOps integration, teams can streamline their workflows and improve software delivery.
        </p>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/conclusion-artifacts.jpg" alt="Azure Artifacts Integration Summary" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Integrating Azure Artifacts simplifies package management in modern CI/CD workflows.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
